jobs.description:
For our client in Kessel, we are looking for a production employee for the Maintenance and Laundry department. In this role, you’ll be responsible for inspecting used materials for quality, cleaning them, packaging, and getting them ready for transport or storage. You'll work with modern machinery to ensure the customer receives rental items that are complete, clean, and undamaged. You’ll be handling various tent components such as floors, walls, doors, windows, and canvases, cleaning them both manually and with machines. Familiarity with industrial machinery and using a high-pressure cleaner is essential.

Your tasks will include:

- Washing and maintaining tent components and rental materials (e.g., floors, walls, doors, windows, and canvases) by machine and hand;
- Operating industrial washers, dryers, high-pressure cleaners, and overhead cranes;
- Monitoring product quality and detecting any damages;
- Inspecting and packing canvases;
- Preparing materials for storage or transport;
- Maintaining a safe and sustainable workspace.

You will be working in an international environment where Dutch and English are the primary languages. Working hours are from 07:00 to 15:30, Monday through Friday.

We are seeking someone with experience in an industrial production setting and a hands-on approach. You’re not afraid to roll up your sleeves and tackle physical tasks. Additionally, you possess:

- A completed VMBO or basic vocational education (level 2) or an equivalent qualification;
- Good command of Dutch or English;
- A forklift certification, or you’re willing to obtain one;
- A desire to grow by participating in internal training opportunities.

Are you looking for a fulltime job in logistics? Would you like to work in a modern, international warehouse where fashion and clothing products are shipped to customers all over the world? Then this opportunity could be perfect for you!

For a large logistics clothing warehouse in Lelystad, we are looking for motivated Production Workers, Warehouse Operatives, and Logistics Associates. You will become part of a friendly international team where teamwork, quality, and a positive working atmosphere are key. On top of that, you can enjoy a delicious hot lunch every working day.

As a Production Worker in the warehouse, you will help ensure that all goods are processed efficiently and accurately. Your tasks will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Picking and packing customer orders;
- Checking products for quality;
- Unpacking boxes and processing incoming goods;
- Sorting clothing and accessories;
- Maintaining a clean and safe working environment.

This is a full-time position in a 2-shift rotation:

- Morning shift: 07:00 AM - 03:30 PM
- Afternoon shift: 03:00 PM - 11:30 PM

But there is also a nightshift you can work if you want from 23:00 tot 07:30. And there is work in the weekends!

- (Basic) English communication skills, or Polish or Spanish;
- Availability for full-time work in a 2-shift schedule;
- Ability to work effectively in a team;
- Physically fit and comfortable performing active warehouse work;
- Attention to detail and ability to follow instructions;
- Previous logistics or warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.

SamenvattingFor our client in Oud-Beijerland, we are looking for experienced machine operators. This is a full-time position in potato production. It is an ideal opportunity for people who want to work in a modern production facility and are looking for stable employment.Over de functieAs a machine operator at our production facility, you will help ensure that the potatoes reach our customers in perfect condition and in the correct portions. You will work together with a team that is responsible for maintaining quality at every stage of the production process.
Your responsibilities will include:
Operating and monitoring production machinery;
Checking the quality of the products produced;
Maintaining order, cleanliness and safety at the workplace;
Working together with the production team and technical department;
Reporting on the progress of the work according to the applicable procedures.

You will work in a 2-shift system. The working hours are:
06:00/07:00 - 15:00/16:00 or 15:00/16:00 - 22:00/23:00
Over het bedrijfPotatoNext aims to be a reliable partner throughout the entire potato supply chain. Their goal is to take away the worries of growers and buyers. Through continuous innovation and smart, efficient production, PotatoNext is working on a future-proof product that provides added value in many areas.
PotatoNext currently operates at the locations of the former companies Nedato and Leo de Kock, respectively in Oud-Beijerland and Purmerend. In the near future, the large facility in Oud-Beijerland will become the heart of our dynamic organization.
Wat wij vragenYou have your own accommodation and transportation to work;
You speak English or Dutch;
You have experience as a machine operator;
You are available to work in a 2-shift system.

